t looks burnt, even when raw. The dark covering forms a crust during a cooking. The marinade is a secret, though some imitations have been developed.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n*1½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] brewed [[cookbook:coffee|coffee]] \n*1 cup [[cookbook:Red Wine|red wine]]\n*½ cup [[cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]]\n*½ cup [[cookbook:molasses|molasses]]\n*⅓ cup [[cookbook:Balsamic vinegar|Balsamic vinegar]]\n*⅓ cup Tamari sauce\n*⅓ cup [[cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] [[cookbook:Chili Powder|chili powder]]\n*6 cloves [[cookbook:garlic|garlic]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Combine all ingredients together to make marinade.\n# Use to marinate meat.\n\n== External Links==\n* [http://sfgate.com/cgi-bin/article.cgi?f=/c/a/2003/02/05/FD122380.DTL San Francisco Chronicle article on Schaub's and Fred Steak]\n* [http://voice.paly.net/view_story.php?mo0de=preview&id=1429 Paly Voice Article on Fred]\n* [http://local.yahoo.com/readreviews?id=21396947& Yahoo Local Review]\n\n[[Category:Californian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chili powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brewed coffee]]\n[[Category:Recipes using molasses]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Fred Steak Marinade","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1½ cup brewed coffee","sourceText":"1½ cup brewed coffee","amountText":"1½ cup brewed coffee","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 cup red wine","sourceText":"1 cup red wine","amountText":"1 cup red wine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ cup olive oil","sourceText":"½ cup olive oil","amountText":"½ cup olive oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ cup molasses","sourceText":"½ cup molasses","amountText":"½ cup molasses","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"⅓ cup Balsamic vinegar","s